  (text "TX AUDIO SELECT - relay switches what reaches the aircraft's mic\njack between ADAU1861's own analog output (AeroNode speaking) and\nthe pilot's boom mic (from the earcup), per Peter 2026-09-29.\n\nK1 = G6K-2F-Y (same qualified relay used on the H1 headset-mute\nboard - bifurcated crossbar contacts, rated for dry-circuit audio,\nNOT a generic silver-contact relay). Only pole A is used; pole B\n(pins 21/22/24) is unused and marked no-connect.\n\nFAIL-PASSIVE CHOICE (mine, not yet confirmed by Peter): de-energized\n(NC, pin 12) = BOOM_MIC_FROM_EARCUP - the pilot's own mic still\nreaches the aircraft if power/control is lost. Energized (NO, pin\n14) = HPOUTP - AeroNode's audio reaches the aircraft mic input only\nwhen actively driven. Confirm this is the wanted default before fab.\n\nQ1/D1/R10 = standard low-side coil driver: GPIO_RLY_TX_SEL_3V3 (a\nnew signal on J1 pin 4, previously spare) -> 2N7002 gate, R10 100k\ngate pulldown for fail-passive (relay stays de-energized if the GPIO\nis high-Z during host boot), D1 flyback diode across the coil.\n\nOPEN ITEMS - not resolved by this pass:\n1. RLY_COIL_SUPPLY has NO SOURCE. G6K-2F-Y is a 5V-coil part; VBAT\n   (5.0-7.3V) would overvolt it. Needs either a dedicated 5V rail or\n   a different coil-voltage variant before this can be built.\n2. HPOUTP is tapped RAW off U1 (no series R/C, no clamp). The H1\n   board's equivalent injection used a 220nF+10k blocking network\n   plus a BAT54S clamp because the far end carries aircraft mic\n   bias (8-16V) that could exceed the ADAU1861's 2.1V abs-max input\n   ceiling. That protection is NOT yet replicated here - do this\n   before connecting to a real aircraft mic circuit.\n3. J5 (3.5mm TRS -> PJ068 adapter) Ring is left NO-CONNECT - bias\n   pass-through from the aircraft to the boom mic capsule is\n   undesigned. Sleeve ties straight to this board's AGND, i.e. NO\n   isolation from aircraft ground (unlike the transformer-isolated\n   H1 board) - flagged, not designed out.\n4. J4 (boom mic from earcup) and J5 are generic placeholders, same\n   convention as J1/J2/J3 on the main sheet - real connectors once\n   the mechanical interface is chosen.\n5. Second transistor/relay pole, footprint for K1 (G6K package is\n   1-8, not the generic Relay_DPDT symbol's EN50005 numbering) -\n   same open item as the H1 board's K1/K2, not resolved here either."
    (at 20 160 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "42a3bbbc-6125-4a56-ba82-2b0a7bea269d")
  )
